From 743878bef455aa4f55fa0ad577f44c29cd047ce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:55:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] Generate actual Krama-patha output for RV 1.1 (all 9
 verses)

The first real output of krama_kramahetu_rules.json, not just rule
data: tools/pratishakhya/generate_krama_rv_1_1.py applies the patala-10
rules (base pairing 10.2, avagrhya/ardharca-final Parigraha 10.7-10.9,
the sthitopasthita word+iti+word mechanism 10.14, the avagraha split in
the repeat 10.16) to all nine verses of RV 1.1, hand-aligned against
DGE's own attested samhita-patha for each pair's sandhi (this project
has no independent sandhi engine -- sandhi is a strictly local
phenomenon, so reading it off the already-correct samhita text is
exact, not approximate).

An earlier version of the generator tried to auto-derive each
Parigraha unit's "combined form" by splitting the pair text on
whitespace -- caught failing whenever sandhi fuses two words with no
visible space, and replaced with an explicit hand-verified
PARIGRAHA_FORMS table instead. Six pairs are explicitly flagged
confidence:"low" where the monosyllable "aa" appears, since sutra 10.3
calls out such monosyllables as behaving specially rather than pairing
forward in the ordinary way -- flagged rather than silently guessed at.

This output is NOT validated against a published Krama-patha edition;
that is the deliberate next step (see the forthcoming verification
packet).

